    EdukSine formerly Pinoy Indie Films Road Show's journey has been punctuated by a string of prestigious recognition that underscore its scientific, technical, and engineering expertise, elevating it as a trailblazer in the technological realm. In 2019, the inception of "Cine Kabundukan" marked a turning point, and its impact was promptly recognized by Animo Labs. The program's visionary spirit earned EdukSine the esteemed Green Archer Innovation Award in 2019, particularly notable within the sphere of Education, Gender, and Inequality. This acknowledgment illuminated EdukSine's dedication to bridging gaps and advocating inclusivity, propelling it to the forefront of transformative endeavors.

    Karen Jane Salutan, the founder and CEO and the driving force behind EdukSine, emerged as a beacon of inspiration, collecting a series of honors that underscored her multifaceted impact. The Benilde Alumni Technopreneur (BEAT) Award of 2019celebrated her dynamic contributions that transcended traditional boundaries.

    On a broader stage, the ASIA CEO AWARDS paid homage to Karen's prowess and dedication. The year 2021 witnessed her ascent as she secured the coveted titles of InLife Circle of Excellence and SHERO of the Year. This recognition of her exemplary leadership and dedication was repeated in 2022, as she stood tall as the Young Leader of the Year within the Circle of Excellence.
