    EdukSine's trajectory of innovation and impact culminated in the establishment of EdukSine Production Corporation, a pivotal step that catapulted Karen into the league of trailblazers. Her visionary enterprise secured a coveted spot in DOST PCIEERED's first cohort of WOMEN-HELPING-WOMEN: INNOVATING SOCIAL ENTERPRISES (WHWise) 2021 Grant and Incubation program. This accolade served as a testament to her ability to intertwine technological innovation with social impact.
    <img>
    The accolades continued to unfold on the global stage. EdukSine's prominence resonated as it secured a place among the finalists of the SHE LOVES TECH PHILIPPINES 2022, a testament to its excellence in the realm of technology. Similarly, the platform's commitment to social change earned it the distinction of being one of the Top 10 Social Enterprises of UNDP ISIP Program, an acknowledgment of its transformative potential.

    On the national front, EdukSine's contributions were heralded by TAYO (Ten Accomplished Youth Organizations) 2023, where it stood as a distinguished National Finalist. The recognition highlighted EdukSine's capacity to drive meaningful impact, especially among the youth.
